00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.130
ERICA CHUONG: Hi, everyone.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.090
I'm Erica Chuong, a customer
engineer at Google Cloud.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.000
Welcome back to Google Cloud
Technical Guides for Startups,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.550
a video series designed for
startup technical enablement

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.890
to help startups to
start, build, and grow

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.380
their businesses
successfully and sustainably

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.940
on Google Cloud.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.860
This episode focuses
on how you can

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.980
make the most of Google Cloud
through various startup offers.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.780
In this video,
we're going to cover

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.790
Google for Startups
Program for startups

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.549
from preseed to series A,
what the program entails,

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:35.910
eligibility requirements, and
best practices, the Migration

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.060
Incentive Program for startups
post-series A on another Cloud

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.270
platform, and best practices
and resources for your startup.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.880
So without any
further ado, let's

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.620
get right into
exploring the benefits

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.930
and resources of Google
for Startups Cloud Program

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:49.650
together.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.320
Our current program supports
your startup's growth

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.050
with Google for
Startups Cloud Program.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.840
Investor-backed startups
get financial, technical,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.310
and business support
that scales with them.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.550
They'll build with
intelligent, cost-effective,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.970
proven technology that can
enable startups to move fast.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.700
As part of the program,
they can upskill their team.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.250
On the technical support
side, our startup success team

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.290
is in place as a
dedicated resource

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.452
to connect with program
members to ensure

00:01:15.452 --> 00:01:17.160
that they have the
technical support they

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:20.190
need to successfully
build their businesses.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.010
This program features access
to our customer engineers

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.810
to help with architecture
reviews, troubleshooting,

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.840
and even invitations
to technical training

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.940
and certification
programs, as well

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.770
as support and documentation.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.720
They can also get
a financial boost.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.790
Startups that are
accepted into the program

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.550
will get their first year
with Google Cloud covered up

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.940
to a total of $100,000 USD.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.600
In year two, they'll get 20%
of Google Cloud usage covered,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.450
also up to $100,000 USD.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.030
This program is designed
to help startups to get off

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.460
the ground when they may
need it the most and then

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.680
on to a sustainable growth
path for the future.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.650
We also see a lot of
startups using credits

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.660
to test new features
or try out products

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.700
such as Looker or Firebase.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.440
Details and conditions
can be found

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.860
at cloud.google.com/startup.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.893
They can also receive
business support.

00:02:09.893 --> 00:02:12.060
You'll get tailored support
from our startup success

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.300
team and our sales teams with
a single point of contact

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.630
to help you navigate Google,
attend special events,

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.180
meet Google engineers
and specialists,

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.550
and even connect
with startup peers

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.460
solving similar challenges
in the Google Cloud startup

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.900
community.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.050
They may even be comarketing
opportunities with startups

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.050
that you can be invited
to cocreate a case study

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.122
or be featured in a blog post.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.580
Now that we've gone over what
the Google for Startups Cloud

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.760
Program is, let's talk
about how to qualify for it.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.240
All customers must be funded
with publicly verifiable equity

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.810
investments up to and
including preseed, angel seed,

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.390
and series A. If
series A, this must

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.760
have been raised within
the past 12 months.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.370
They must also have been founded
within 10 years of applying

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.070
to the program and have a
publicly available company

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.950
website and a unique
company email domain.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.380
If you need to create
a custom email account,

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.420
sign up for Google Workspace.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.540
You must also have a valid
Google Cloud billing account

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.580
ID linked to the
domain and company

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.990
email on your application.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.870
Additionally, a
customer must not

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.270
be already enrolled in the
Google for Startups Cloud

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:22.350
Program or have received
in excess of $4,000 USD

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.540
in Google Cloud credits.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.050
You must also not be a company
who has IPOed or been acquired

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.380
or an educational institution,
government entity,

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.090
nonprofit, personal blog, dev
shop, consultancy, or agency.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.600
You must also not be a crypto
mining company or a company

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.750
distributing tokens contrary
to regulatory guidance

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.310
in your jurisdiction.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.590
For example, companies
issuing tokens solely

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:49.620
for speculative purposes
will not be considered.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.010
Apply at
cloud.google.com/startup

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.500
and accept the program
terms and conditions.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.510
Your application will
be routed for review

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.280
to ensure we can
validate your identity

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.170
and confirm eligibility.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.910
If accepted, credits
are activated

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.160
in the billing account
provided in the application.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.780
And an email
notification is sent

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.810
to the applicant with an
overview of the program.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.580
If we cannot accept
your application,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.010
an email notification is sent
to the applicant with more

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:17.040
information and guidance on
how to remedy the issues.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.779
Google for Startups
Cloud credits

00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:21.720
carry the same scope as most
other Cloud credit programs

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.040
in 2022.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.920
They can be used for Google
Cloud Services like BigQuery

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:26.850
and Cloud Run.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:29.220
It can also be used for other
offerings, such as Looker

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.420
and Actifio.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.800
In addition, these
credits can be

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.237
used for Firebase
and support services.

00:04:34.237 --> 00:04:35.820
Check out the links
in the description

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.075
box below for more details.

00:04:38.075 --> 00:04:39.450
Google for Startups
Cloud credits

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.240
will not cover the cost
of third-party marketplace

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.620
licenses.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:46.890
Workspace, Maps, and Qwiklabs
benefits are managed separately

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.750
and can be redeemed
by eligible startups

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:52.350
by emailing
Cloudstartupsupport@google.com.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.010
Let's go over some best
practices for your application.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.260
Verifying your identity
is the first step

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.050
to apply for Google for
Startups Cloud Program.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.900
This process helps us to
protect you and your company

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.020
and ensure the correct startups
are enrolling in the program.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.870
Here are some pro tips to
help us do this step quickly

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.340
and efficiently.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.740
Apply with your startup's
business email address,

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:14.910
not a personal one.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.240
For example, use
app@coolstartup.com, not

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.550
coolstartup@gmail.com.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.620
Ensure your email address
and business domain

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.870
on the application matches.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.810
Next, provide an active
Google Cloud billing ID.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.460
Example on the screen.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.100
Make sure that you have an
individual Google Cloud billing

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.400
ID that is just for
your singular company.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.230
While we're on the
subject of billing IDs,

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.050
use a billing ID that
your company controls.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.900
The owner of the billing account
must have the same email domain

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.740
as the email and domain
used on the application.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.240
Check your startup's funding.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.880
Your startup must have
received preseed to series

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.020
A equity funding.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.850
And if series A,
that funding must

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.030
have occurred within one year
of applying to that program.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.150
Provide documentation of
equity investments via publicly

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.190
available online sources.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.730
Examples include reputable news
articles, investment aggregator

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.940
sites, and investment
portfolio posts.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.370
We can not accept
confidential information

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.610
and/or social media posts
from your own company.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.380
Please remember to double check
all parts of the application

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:19.920
and eligibility requirements
prior to submitting.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.270
And with that,
you're ready to go.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.330
If your startup
is beyond series A

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.060
and looking to migrate across
from another cloud provider

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.820
or on-prem system,
this migration program

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.500
is the program for you.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.030
Our migration
incentive program is

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.070
designed to support
later-stage startups

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:38.040
by offsetting costs of
migrating cloud services

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.900
and infrastructure
to Google Cloud.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.130
Startups will receive high-touch
technical support to both plan

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.410
and execute the
migration and access

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.480
to instructor-led
and online training

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.910
to help ensure your team
has the required technical

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.290
capabilities.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.810
Our Google Cloud engineers
and ecosystem partners

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:57.780
are ready to support you
and your migration journey.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.900
Other benefits, such as
Google Workspace, Google Maps,

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.850
and Google Cloud
Skills Boost benefits

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.470
are also offered
to these startups.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.210
And your account
manager will support you

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:09.030
in benefiting from these
incentives and beyond.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.880
To learn more about the
migration incentive program,

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.590
please reach out to
your dedicated sales

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.450
team who could be
your personal guide

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.190
throughout the entire process.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.900
You can be connected
to your sales team

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:22.380
at cloud.google.com/contacts.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.380
Apply for the Google for
Startups Cloud Program today.

